    content: "Arrays and loops work together for most array operations.\n\nSum of Array:\nint arr[5] = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};\nint sum = 0;\nfor (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {\n    sum += arr[i];\n}\ncout << \"Sum: \" << sum;  // 150\n\nFind Maximum:\nint arr[5] = {3, 7, 2, 9, 5};\nint maxVal = arr[0];\nfor (int i = 1; i < 5; i++) {\n    if (arr[i] > maxVal) {\n        maxVal = arr[i];\n    }\n}\ncout << \"Max: \" << maxVal;  // 9\n\nCount Occurrences:\nint arr[7] = {1, 2, 3, 2, 4, 2, 5};\nint count = 0;\nfor (int i = 0; i < 7; i++) {\n    if (arr[i] == 2) count++;\n}\ncout << \"2 appears \" << count << \" times\";  // 3\n\nReverse Array:\nint arr[5] = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};\nfor (int i = 0; i < 5 / 2; i++) {\n    swap(arr[i], arr[4 - i]);\n}\n// arr is now {5, 4, 3, 2, 1}\n\nLinear Search:\nint arr[5] = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};\nint target = 30;\nint index = -1;\nfor (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {\n    if (arr[i] == target) {\n        index = i;\n        break;\n    }\n}\ncout << \"Found at index: \" << index;  // 2",
