    content: "std::string is a class that handles text in C++.\n\n#include <string>\n\nDeclaring Strings:\nstring s1 = \"Hello\";\nstring s2(\"World\");\nstring s3 = s1 + \" \" + s2;  // \"Hello World\"\nstring s4(5, 'a');            // \"aaaaa\"\n\nCommon Operations:\nstring s = \"Hello\";\n\ns.length();       // 5 (number of characters)\ns.size();         // 5 (same as length())\ns.empty();        // false\ns[0];             // 'H' (first character)\ns.at(0);          // 'H' (bounds-checked)\ns.front();        // 'H'\ns.back();         // 'o' (last character)\n\nConcatenation:\nstring first = \"Hello\";\nstring second = \" World\";\nstring result = first + second;  // \"Hello World\"\n\nfirst += \"!\";  // \"Hello!\" (append)\nfirst.append(\"?\");  // \"Hello!?\" (append)\n\nSubstring:\nstring s = \"Hello World\";\ns.substr(0, 5);     // \"Hello\" (start, length)\ns.substr(6);        // \"World\" (from index 6 to end)\n\nFind:\nstring s = \"Hello World\";\ns.find(\"World\");    // 6 (index of first occurrence)\ns.find(\"xyz\");      // string::npos (not found)\n\nComparison:\nstring a = \"apple\";\nstring b = \"banana\";\nif (a < b) { ... }  // Lexicographic comparison ('a' < 'b')\n\nString Input:\nstring name;\ncin >> name;           // Reads one word\ncin >> ws;             // Discard whitespace\ngetline(cin, name);    // Reads entire line",
